<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mahamati Prannath</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1618">1618</a>–<a href="/years/1694">1694</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> · Also known as Prannath</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mahamati Prannath was a religious teacher from Jamnagar in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gujarat">Gujarat</a> who led the Pranami sect, a Krishna-centred devotional movement founded by his guru Devchandra. He travelled widely, preaching against religious division, and settled at Panna as guru of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bundela">Bundela</a> ruler <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chhatrasal">Chhatrasal</a>, whom he encouraged in his struggle against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mughal-empire">Mughals</a>. His teachings were collected in the Tartam Sagar, and Panna remains the sect's chief centre.</p></div>
